# Allowlist of email addresses that may appear in this repo's file contents.
#
# SHA-256 of the lowercased address, never the address itself — writing them in
# clear would make this file the largest collection of personal data in the repo,
# which is the opposite of the point. The comment after each hash says where the
# address was found, so this stays reviewable.
#
# Everything here is inherited from upstream (Radarr/Sonarr contributors, NLog and
# Sentry config, test fixtures) or is the project's own noreply address. Anything
# NOT on this list fails scripts/check-personal-email.sh.
#
# Add an entry only for an address that genuinely belongs in the tree:
#   printf '%s' 'someone@example.com' | shasum -a 256
